{title: 168 - And Have the Bright Immensities}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #168 • FOREST GREEN • 8.6.7.5.8.6.8.6}
{lyricist: Howard C. Robbins}
{composer: Traditional English melody}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 168}
{meta: tune FOREST GREEN}
{meta: meter 8.6.7.5.8.6.8.6}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]And [Dm/A]have [Bb]the [C7/Bb]bright immensities
[F]Received [Bb]our [F/C]risen [Gm/D]Lord,
[C7/Bb]Where light [Dm/A]years [C]frame [Dm/A]the [Bb]Pleiades
[C7/Bb]And point Orion’s [F]sword?
[F]Do flaming suns His [Gm/D]footsteps [Dm/A]trace
[Dm/A]Thro’ corridors [C7]sublime,
[C7/Bb]The Lord [Am]of [F]interstellar space
[F]And conqueror [C/E]of time?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]The [Dm/A]heav'n [Bb]that [F/C]hides [C7]Him from [F]our sight
[F]Knows neither near nor [Gm/D]far;
[C7/Bb]A little [C]candle [Dm/A]sheds [Bb]its [F/C]light
[C7/Bb]As surely [F]as a [C/G]star.
[F]And where [Bb]His [F/C]loving [Gm/D]people [Dm/A]meet
[Dm/A]To share [Am]the [F]gift [C7]divine,
[C7/Bb]There stands [Am]He [F]with unhurrying feet;
[F]There heav'nly splendors [C/E]shine.
{end_of_verse}
